TCP transfer network protocol

tcp 3 way handshake is a connection established between the client and the server before they exchange the data

when your browser connects to a website using HTTPS, TCP establishes a connection before TLS and HTTP data are exchanged (in the usual TCP-based HTTPS setup).

the three steps invlude
SYN
SYN-ACK
ACK

lets say the client send its initial sequence number SYN=100
then the server acknowledges the sequence number and send it's own sequence number
in the step of SYN-ACK
SYN=500,ACK=101

the client acknowledges the sequqnce number of the server 
ACK=501

Reasons:

it is used to established a connection between the client and server
this is used to detect missing data and reorder the messages and avoid delivering duplicate data
to ensure the communication is is there in both the sides
to prevent problems caused by delayed communication